course: dictionary
lesson: 5088
title: Words about thinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone is thinking, not how they look or move. «Intellectually» is one of these words. It comes from «intellect», which means the mind's power to think, reason and understand, so it is about using your brain.
explain: The word has two meanings. First, it means in a way that uses thinking and reasoning: «The puzzle was intellectually challenging, so Maya thought for a long time.» Second, it means in the mind, rather than in the body or the feelings: «The debate was won intellectually, by clear reasoning and not by shouting.»
explain: To check a meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. Could you say "in a way that uses thinking" instead? If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. The words beside it, such as challenging, curious or honest, are the clues.
fact: «Intellectually» means in a way that uses thinking, reasoning and understanding.
fact: «Intellectually» can also mean in the mind, rather than in the body or the feelings.
fact: «Intellectually challenging» means something that makes you think hard.
fact: «Intellectually curious» describes someone who wants to learn and wonder about ideas.
fact: «Intellectually honest» means truthful about what you really think and what the evidence shows.
exercise: «The maths puzzle was intellectually challenging.» What does intellectually mean here? | In a way that needs strong muscles | In a loud and noisy way | *In a way that needs hard thinking | In a hurry, without any thought
exercise: Ella says, «I am intellectually curious about space.» What does she mean? | She has a space helmet | *She wants to learn and understand ideas about space | She is scared of the dark | She has a sore head
exercise: «Her answer was intellectually honest: she said she was not sure.» What does intellectually honest mean? | Very fast at answering | Happy that she won | Loud and proud of herself | *Truthful about what she really thinks
test: «Solving the riddle was an intellectually satisfying task for Sam.» What does intellectually suggest here? | Using his hands to paint | Using his legs to run | Using his stomach to digest | *Using his mind and reasoning
test: «The debate was won intellectually, not by shouting.» What is being contrasted? | Friends rather than enemies | Hard exercise rather than thinking | Bright colours rather than shapes | *Clear thinking and reasoning rather than loud voices
exam: Dad said, «The quiz was intellectually demanding, so the whole family had to think hard.» What does intellectually demanding mean? | Needing a lot of food | Needing a loud shout | *Needing a lot of careful thought | Needing a lot of sleep
